done-so-far: slice 1 matches the Rust routes on ALL 1884 cells present on disk (status + every field), and /view matches byte-for-byte on a live and a revoked token, headers included. Commit 05e70a5 fixed four gaps in /view that status-parity had hidden: it served index.html instead of view.html (580KB vs 27KB, both 200), never injected window._VIEW_TOKEN (a 200 carrying a console that could not call anything), answered 200 instead of 404 for a missing file, and answered an expired link with raw JSON instead of the styled page. Also aligned Content-Type on every JSON answer (unstated, the runtime guessed text/plain for a JSON body) and put `ok: false` back in the 400 body.
next: the switch lives in the gateway on branch feature/matrix-task-info-single-source (dc8b029): ROZUM_UCC_SSC_ORIGIN picks which implementation registers the two routes; unset = today's behaviour exactly, unreachable .ssc = 502 (never a silent fallback to Rust). Both branches are committed and unmerged, and NOTHING live has been switched — the deployment decisions (install the binary, set the variable, supervise the .ssc process) are the operator's.
deploy-order: tasks.json MUST be in the deployed checkout BEFORE the new gateway binary. matrix_task_info resolves it against the process working directory (launchd sets /Users/sergiy/work/my/rozum), so a binary deployed first serves null prompts that look like data. It now says so once in the log instead of staying quiet.
deviation: the .ssc runtime adds `Cache-Control: no-store` to every answer; the Rust routes send none on these two. Kept — harmless on an authorized read — but it is the ONE header that differs.
debt (CORRECTED 2026-08-13 — the earlier note would have caused a regression):
  - isInt's two local copies CAN go. Their &String/&f64 arms are in scalascript main now (they wrote
    their own patch from my report rather than merging my branch), and `s.toInt.toString == s`
    compiles and answers true/false/false. Do it in the same change that drops the comment.
  - isNumeric's dot-splitting MUST STAY. My earlier note said it existed only because `toDouble` on
    a String emitted an invalid cast — that is wrong and following it would break the slice. The
    real reason is that Rust prints `8.0_f64` as "8", so `"8.0".toDouble.toString == "8.0"` is FALSE
    and the field silently stays a quoted string. That is a property of the target, not a defect
    they can fix. The comment beside the code says this correctly; this note did not.
  - viewRoute inserts via split + a hand-rolled join, and every concatenation joins exactly two
    operands, because build-rust lowers indexOf on a String to .iter().position(…) and a
    list-element + top-level-val concatenation to String + String. Filed.
  - the slice's isInt CANNOT run on the `run` lane against real data: `"8.0".toInt` ABORTS there
    (`String.toInt: invalid integer`) while build-rust answers 0. Filed. Exercise the slice on
    build-rust only until that is settled.
upstream-recheck 2026-08-14 (second pass, MEASURED not grepped): both blockers still stand.
  (1) BUILD. Their `std/http.ssc` DECLARES `route(method, path, handler: Request => Response)`
  and a `Response` type — the API is right in main. `build-rust` still lowers the callback to
  `Box<dyn Fn(..) -> String>`, so the slice fails to compile: two `E0308: expected String, found
  Response` at the two route registrations. A declaration honoured by one lane and not the other,
  which is the same shape as every other defect filed from here. Not staleness — `ResponseParts`
  is absent from their main and no rebuild changes an API gap.
  (2) BIND. `SSC_HTTP_BIND` appears in their main only inside INBOX.md, my own report.
  There is no rozum-side workaround for (1): returning a bare String body is exactly the shape
  that cannot answer 400/404/410, and this slice's whole claim is that it refuses with a status.
